<div class="number">
    <span class="digits">19.</span>
</div>
<div class="metadata">
    <div class="info" >
        <div class="subinfo">
            <h3>
                <span class="title"><a target="_parent" href="/coa/coa/en/item/18759/index.do?q=%22Crown+Liability+and+Proceedings+Act%2C+2019%22">The Catalyst Capital Group Inc. v. Dundee Kilmer Developments Limited Partnership</a></span>
                        - <span class="citation">2020 ONCA 272</span>
                - <span class="publicationDate">2020-04-29</span>
            </h3>
            <div class="subMetadata">
                <span>Decisions of the Court of Appeal</span>
                    - <span>Civil</span>
            </div> 
            <div class="subject">
            </div> 
                <p class="snippet" >
                    [107] Given that conclusion, it is not necessary to address the submissions of the respondents that the enactment of s. 11 of the <b>Crown Liability and Proceedings Act, 2019</b>, S.O. 2019, c. 7, Sched. 17, extinguished in Ontario the kind of public law claim described by Stratas J.A. in Paradis Honey. 
                </p>
